  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Thai narrative recitation in which a solo reciter delivers verse from the epic Khun Chang Khun Phaen, keeping time with krap sepha, two pairs of hardwood bars clicked together in each hand. In the early Bangkok period a piphat sepha ensemble was added to play pieces between passages of recitation, and its repertoire became part of the Thai classical canon. An auxiliary-percussion card stands in for the krap sepha and a generic drum card for the ensemble drum.",
